<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland to get 180 new jobs - minister.</title>
<headline>Ireland to get 180 new jobs - minister.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's Enterprise and Employment Minister Richard Bruton said on Thursday approval had been given for the expansion of two electronic manufacturing plants in Cork which will create 180 new jobs within the next three years.</p>
<p>The IDA Ireland-assisted expansions include a 5.6 million Irish punt investment by DOVatron Ireland B.V. which will generate 100 new jobs within the next three years to bring total employment at the plant to 420 people.</p>
<p>DOVatron Ireland is part of the Colorado-based DII Group Inc.</p>
<p>Moog Limited, a wholly owned subsidiary of New York's Moog Inc, plans to invest 4.4 million Irish pounds to create 80 jobs, this will bring the total employment at the plant to 168 in two years, Bruton said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
</text>
